{"availability":"available","full":"0xEmmo/third-mainland","name":"third-mainland","description":"GPU-rendered night map of how Lagos moves through a day: 40k particles on real OSM roads, BRT, rail and ferries. three.js WebGPU + WebGL 2 fallback, React, TypeScript, PWA.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-11T16:29:01Z","updated":"2026-10-11T17:28:41Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://third-mainland.vercel.app","topics":["accessibility","data-visualization","lagos","maps","openstreetmap","pwa","react","threejs","typescript","vite","webgl","webgpu"],"demo":"https://third-mainland.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:47.401Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:47.401Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:50:47.401Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:50:47.401Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A GPU-rendered night map of how Lagos moves through a day. Forty thousand particles flow along the city's real roads, BRT lanes, rail lines and ferry routes, thickening into amber jams on Third Mainland Bridge at 07:40 and thinning out to a trickle at midnight. Scrub the day, switch to a Saturday or a rain day, and every corridor's speed, journey time and timetable updates with it.","Live: third-mainland.vercel.app · Built by Emmanuel Balogun","Illustrative, not live traffic. The lines are traced from OpenStreetMap; the flows on them come from a hand-tuned model of a Lagos day. The app says so on screen, too."],"features":["Scrub the day. Drag the demand histogram, use the arrow keys, or jump to the morning peak, midday,","Change the kind of day. Weekday, Saturday (midday market peak, thinner timetables) or a rain day","Filter by mode. The legend is also the layer switch: road, BRT, ferry and rail.","Sort by slowest, busiest or A–Z, with a speed sparkline for the selected corridor.","Pan, pinch, scr